        "setup": null,
        "description": "Assemble colmap4d components with array validation and byte-preserving binary copies; optional full strict validation.",
        "category": [
          "reconstruction",
          "colmap4d"
        ],
        "docs": "Uses colmap4d.arrays.read_point_arrays and read_image_headers. No Python Point3D/observation objects on the canonical uniform-track binary fast path. Binary files and pixels are independently copied unchanged; IDs, observations and int64 ns are preserved. Default fast validation is not a validate_full certification: single-track reciprocity is exhaustive; multi-track reciprocity/centroids sample up to 4096 points and observations per image. All records receive structure, geometry, ID, time-coverage and bounds checks. strict_validate=true and text/nonuniform-layout fallbacks retain the legacy complete validator and final validate_full(strict). No library modifications, XMP inference, timestamp changes or hardlinks. See README.md for coverage and performance evidence.",
        "source_entry": "merge_colmap4d.py",
        "arrayable": false,
        "parallelism": null,
        "batch_size": null,
